<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Dear&nbsp;{!Contact.FirstName},</span></font><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div><div><font face="arial">We are pleased to inform you that you have passed your audition on INSTRUMENT and are now accepted as a Music Performance Minor in the School of Music in the Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts at Arizona State University. If you have not already done so, please review the Music Performance Minor course requirements <a href="http://music.asu.edu/students/undergrad/nonmajors.php">here</a>.&nbsp;</font></div><div><font face="arial">&nbsp;</font></div><div><font face="arial">To officially add the minor, please contact your major area advisor to schedule an appointment. You should bring this letter as confirmation that you are admitted into the Music Performance Minor. &nbsp;</font></div><div><br></div><div><font face="arial">Sincerely,</font></div></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: arial; font-size: 12pt;"><div><b style="font-size: 12pt;">Julie Stephens</b></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><div><font face="arial" color="#999999">Coordinator, Academic Affairs + Admissions</font></div><div><font face="arial"><b><font color="#990000">Arizona State University</font>&nbsp;|&nbsp;</b></font><b style="color: rgb(255, 204, 0); font-size: 12pt;">Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts&nbsp;</b></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(153, 153, 153);">P.O. Box 870405 |&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(153, 153, 153);">Tempe, Arizona 85287-0405</span></div><div><font color="#999999">Phone: 480-965-5069</font></div><div><span style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-size: 12pt;">{!Case.Thread_Id}</span></div></div></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>